Source: gimlet-eye-toolkit
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gimlet Eye maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
# The engine is Rust; the CLI and the desktop frontend are TypeScript, so a
# build needs both toolchains. scripts/rehearse-upgrade.sh installs rustup and
# node into a container to prove that.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc, nodejs (>= 20), npm
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/James-HoneyBadger/GimletEye
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/James-HoneyBadger/GimletEye.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: gimlet
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 20), gimlet-engine (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: gnupg
Description: local workbench for system, crypto, and metadata tasks
 One tool registry, one report format, one configuration file, one audit trail,
 and one command line for system administration, file encryption and signing,
 and metadata removal.
 .
 Everything runs locally: no network calls, no telemetry, no auto-update.

Package: gimlet-engine
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: verified crypto and metadata engine for Gimlet Eye
 The Rust engine behind the Gimlet Eye command line and desktop app. It carries
 the fuzz corpora, the golden fixtures, and a second implementation that pins
 the container format, and it runs only the tools this build compiled.
 .
 It is spawned by the surfaces over a versioned JSON protocol and is not
 intended to be invoked directly.
